<HelpTab>
    <HelpSection Title="Writing messages">
        <ul>
            <li>Press Enter to send and Shift+Enter for a new line. On a phone, Return adds a line and the Send
                button sends.</li>
            <li>Use the formatting buttons for bold, italic, strikethrough, lists and links.</li>
            <li>A message can be up to 4,000 characters.</li>
        </ul>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="New messages">
        <FluentText>
            New messages appear in an open conversation as soon as they're sent, with no need to reload. While the
            conversation is on screen, they count as read a moment after they arrive. If you use a screen reader, it
            reads out each new message from someone else: who sent it and the start of what it says.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Replying, editing and deleting">
        <FluentText>Open the … menu on a message:</FluentText>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Reply</strong> quotes it above your next message.</li>
            <li><strong>Edit</strong> changes one of your own messages. It's marked "edited".</li>
            <li><strong>Delete</strong> removes one of your own messages for everyone. It shows as "Message deleted".</li>
        </ul>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Pinned posts and shift cards">
        <FluentText>
            Managers can pin important posts to the top of a channel. Everyone in the channel is notified, even if
            they've muted it. Location channels also show open shifts and swap requests, with a link to pick them up.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Notifications">
        <FluentText>
            You get a notification for new messages in conversations you're not looking at, unless you've muted
            them. If messages sit unread for a day, you get one email a day listing which conversations have
            unread messages. It never includes what they say. Choose what you get on your
            <a href="/account/manage">account page</a>.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>
</HelpTab>
